                                  PReSENtS

                    OPeRAtORPaGER v1.04 BY STATiC/THERioN


=============================================================================
                                 SHORT INFO
=============================================================================

I think you all know what a pager is so i don't think there is a need to
specific the description. What is so special about this pager you might say,
well... This one is totaly configurabe not like all the other ones available,
some funktions are: Show text when chat flag is on/off, directly comment when
chat flag i off, write your own string to callerslog, etc. lot's of small
options. Do check tooltype information for all funktions.


=============================================================================
                                INSTALLATION
=============================================================================

....2.xx

1. Copy BBS/Doors/Pager/ to Doors:Pager/
2. Modify your custom-commands and add the following line:

*O        XM010Doors:Pager/Pager

^         ^    ^
|         |    `--> Or wherever you put the door door.
|         |
|         `---> Notice the "X", Thiz door is a pure XIM door!
|
`-------> The name to run.

....3.xx

1. Copy BBS/Doors/Pager/ to Doors:Pager/
2. Copy BBS/Commands/BBSCMD/ to BBS:Commands/BBSCMD/



=============================================================================
                           TOOLTYPE CONFIGURATION
=============================================================================

    [!] INDEPENDENT FUNKTION         [X] IN NEED OF ANOTHER FUNKTION(S)

                    [*] TURNS OFF SOME OF THE FUNKTIONS


HOME=<Path:Textfile>        [!]  Will show <Textfile> if chat flag is ON.

NOT_HOME=<Path:Textfile>    [!]  Will show <Textfile> if chat flag is OFF.

USE_DEFAULTS                [*]  Default mode, prompts for chat reason:

        IE:  Enter chat reason (50 chars/One row)..
            (----*----*----*----*----*----*----*----*----*----)

GET_REASON=<Nr>             [!]  This is 4 all sysops that wanna add their
                                 own design when having an input, add the
                                 design at the end of 'HOMETXT', Nr is
                                 numbers of chars to allow.

REASON_STR=<Str>            [X]  When 'GET_REASON=<Nr>' is added Str will b
                                 put b4 input at the same row.
                                 IE: 'REASON_STR=        >'

PASSWORDSTR.<Ax>=<Str>      [!]  Use a password for users with access ?, Str
                                 is the password string 2 use.

EXECUTE_COMMAND.<Ax>=<Str>  [*]  Execute a command, if u wanna have a
                                 sampling played when users with access ?
                                 pages. IE: 'EXECUTE_COMMAND.10=c:Play Samp'
                                 This funktion turs the ordinary paging off.

EXECUTE_COMMENT=<Str>       [X]  When 'EXECUTE_COMMAND.<Ax>=<Str>' exists
                                 Str is string 2 show after command is
                                 executed.

PROMPT_COMMENT              [!]  b4 leaving a comment when chat flag is off
                                 the pager will ask if u wanna leave a
                                 comment 4 the sysop.

PROMPT_STR=<Str>            [X]  When 'PROMPT_COMMENT' exists this is the
                                 String 2 be put as a prompt. ' (Y/N)?' will
                                 b added in the end of the String.

STRING_YES=<Str>            [X]  When 'PROMPT_COMMENT' exists this is the
                                 String 2 be put when answer is 'y'.

STRING_NO=<Str>             [X]  When 'PROMPT_COMMENT' exists this is the
                                 String 2 be put when answer is 'n'.

WRITE_CALLERSLOG=<Str>      [!]  String 2 b put in callerslog when trying 2
                                 page. This will take effect even when chat
                                 flag is off.

NOTE: There is no need 2 add any of this tooltypes.


